{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjXL2iU28wDyaZjdqXrp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VeP9oSuiNrPvpLM5GLa1R9","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"Start: G clef and C time, marked f. Two 16ths before the first bar line (G5, E5) form bar 0, the pickup. Bar 1: three trilled eighth-note figures fall C5 to G4 to E4, each with its two 16ths. Then the low C4–E4 / G3–B3 16th pairs with staccato dots. Bar line. Bar 2: two more beats of C4/E4, G3/B3 pairs, written with abbreviation strokes. Then a lone C4 eighth, rests, p, the 32nd-note run E5–F5 into G5, and a staccato G5. Bar line. Bar 3: G5 eighth, rests, another 32nd run up to G5, G5, then G#5 (the sharp is visible) to A5, A5 staccato eighth, rest. Bar line. Bar 4: 16th rest, slurred F5–E5–D5 run, D5, then the slurred D5–E5–F5–D5 16ths. The line stops there. The rest of bar 4 (grace D5, E5, C5, the last run) must be on the next line. Nothing conflicts with the edition.","right":true,"insights":"Matching was easy. The pickup, the falling trill figures and the sharp on G#5 pin bars 0 to 3, and the bar lines are clear. The ending was the hard part: the line breaks partway through bar 4, and the 16ths at the right edge are small and crowded. A sharper image of the line's last group would have confirmed the break point more quickly."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5535,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5535},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"942a4822-07a5-4499-a4ab-b169e4b081ae","uuid":"c9e84452-a821-4e50-9cac-cf0e4c260afd","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:12:45.396Z","req